      "content": "That's an interesting range of perspectives. You mentioned the idea of certain populations having more \"efficient\" brains or even the more extreme \"white gene\" hypothesis. To keep this grounded in the academic debate, how do proponents of these biological models typically justify the existence of these specific clusters? For instance, what kind of evolutionary mechanisms or selection pressures do they cite to explain why intelligence or cognitive efficiency would manifest differently across these specific ancestral lines?",
